### Page 1 of 2

```text
RESOLUTION NO.______

ENTITLED: “A RESOLUTION ACKNOWLEDGING RECEIPT OF THE
STRATEGIC DOWNTOWN ACTION PLAN ‘HISTORIC
PLACEMAKING: STRATEGIES FOR INVIGORATING DOWNTOWN
CHEYENNE’ AS A WORKING DOCUMENT & TOOL FOR
DOWNTOWN CHEYENNE.”

WHEREAS,  the City of Cheyenne Planning Office is charged with long range planning
efforts for the City of Cheyenne, which includes the area referenced as Downtown Cheyenne; and

WHEREAS,  the City Planning Office conducted the “Buildings, Business and Bankers:
Partnerships for Preservation Conference” in October 2010 to advance momentum for community
development and preservation in the downtown area; the conference featured preservation consultant
Dana Crawford who addressed the pressing need for redevelopment of Downtown Cheyenne; and

WHEREAS,  the City Planning Office submitted and received Certified Local Government
Grant (CLG) #56-11-00000.05 in the amount of $28,500 as an immediate follow-up to the “Buildings,
Business & Bankers – Partnerships for Preservation” conference for the purpose of producing a series
of strategic reports designed to maximize successful implementation of community-identified strategic
goals for advancing downtown historic placemaking; and

WHEREAS,  the City Planning Office hired the joint team of Economic Stewardship Inc. and
Heritage Designs in March 2011 to prepare the strategic downtown action plan to serve as a work plan
to help guide downtown development by identifying strategies that create an action agenda and offer
leaders, downtown stakeholders and citizen partners a menu of opportunities to get involved in helping
to improve and revitalize Cheyenne’s downtown; and

WHEREAS,  the strategies in Historic Placemaking: Strategies for Invigorating Downtown
Cheyenne reflect information and ideas contributed by 428 Cheyenne and Laramie County citizens
who attended 107 meetings and eight public work sessions, offering hundreds of excellent suggestions
about how to think about and respond to the issues affecting Cheyenne’s central business district; and

WHEREAS, the Historic Placemaking: Strategies for Invigorating Downtown Cheyenne
recognizes that downtown Cheyenne must function as a system and is organized by seven issue/action
categories developed as the “things to do” recommendations made by downtown stakeholders: Help
Businesses Succeed, Enhance the Public Realm, Attract Diverse Markets, Rehabilitate Historic
Structures, Catalyze New Developments, Make Downtown Sparkle, and Recruit Businesses
Downtown, and sets forth 41 strategies associated with the seven categories that were also developed
in consultation with downtown stakeholders; and

WHEREAS, implementation of this plan will require the cooperation and assistance of partner
organizations and groups, including: City of Cheyenne, Downtown Development Authority, Cheyenne
Historic Preservation Board, Cheyenne MPO, and Laramie County; and

WHEREAS, the Cheyenne Downtown Development Authority reviewed and accepted the
Historic Placemaking: Strategies for Invigorating Downtown Cheyenne as a planning tool at their
meeting on November 8, 2012; and
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne Planning Commission held a Public Meeting following a
45-day advertised comment period on November 19, 2012, and accepted public comments, and
acknowledged receipt of the Historic Placemaking: Strategies for Invigorating Downtown Cheyenne
at their meeting on November 19, 2012, as a working plan for downtown and recommended the report
proceed to the Governing Body with Planning Commission comments; and

WHEREAS, the Historic Placemaking: Strategies for Invigorating Downtown Cheyenne will
be used as the action agenda to guide and shape the improvement and revitalization of downtown
Cheyenne.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING:

THAT, the City of Cheyenne Governing Body hereby acknowledges receipt of the strategic
downtown action plan Historic Placemaking: Strategies for Invigorating Downtown Cheyenne, dated
Summer 2013, prepared by Economic Stewardship Inc. and Heritage Designs, as a working document
and tool for downtown Cheyenne.

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that the Governing Body recommends that the Historic
Placemaking: Strategies for Invigorating Downtown Cheyenne be used as the action agenda to guide
and shape the improvement and revitalization of downtown Cheyenne.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED THIS ____ DAY OF ___________, 2013.

____________________________
Richard L. Kaysen, Mayor
City of Cheyenne

(Seal)

ATTEST:

____________________________
Carol A. Intlekofer, City Clerk
```
